         <listPerson>
            <person xml:id="JER05" sex="1">
               <persName>
                  <forename>Thomas</forename>
                  <surname>Jervis</surname>
               </persName>
               <birth when="1748-01-13"></birth>
               <death when="1833-08-31"></death>
               <occupation>Unitarian Minister</occupation>
               <occupation>Author</occupation>
               <note type="editorial">
                  <p>Thomas Jervis DNB 1748-1833</p>
                  <p>Godwin encounters both Tho. Jervis and Sw. Jervis in the early 1800s. Ed Pope suggests Thomas Jervis for most of the encounters with a 'Jervis' and identifies <persName key ="JER06">Swynfen Jervis</persName>  for the 7/1/1802 entry. Following this, and in keeping with the fact that many of the more ambigious entries are with a group of Unitarian figures, all unspecified entries for Jervis between 1798 and 1813 have coded to Thomas Jervis.</p>
               </note>
               <bibl type="website">Ed Pope History (26/02/2013)</bibl>
               <bibl type="other">DNB</bibl>
            </person>
         </listPerson>
      </body>   
